Good afternoon,

We are instructed to notify a serious incident on behalf of our client Cobalt Ridge Utility Contractors, LLC. Our reference is OMI/CAS/2026/0033. This is issued under their HSE procedure within 24 hours of a serious incident and we are placing all potentially relevant carriers on notice.

Broker reference: OMI/CAS/2026/0033
Insured name: Cobalt Ridge Utility Contractors, LLC
Contract number: OP-2026-SS-14
Date of loss: 19 May 2026
Loss location: 2200 block of West Carbondale Avenue, Overland Park, KS 66214
Cause: Excavation collapse beyond the end of the trench box
Estimated loss: USD 1,150,000

The north wall of a fourteen-foot excavation failed at a point beyond the trench
box where the crew had extended it to expose an unmarked lateral. Two employees
were buried to chest height and were extricated within 22 and 41 minutes. Both
are admitted; one has a pelvic fracture and a crush injury to the lower leg. A
third was cut during the rescue and released. No fatalities.

The collapse undermined about 40 feet of public sidewalk and a lane of West
Carbondale Avenue, took the support out from under a gas service to the adjacent
retail centre, and fractured the existing sewer - about 9,000 gallons went into
the storm system. OSHA Region VII and KDHE are both notified.

There is no builder's risk and no owner-controlled programme on this contract. It
is a City contract with our client as prime, so their own placements are the ones
engaged: liability, excess, workers compensation, contractors equipment, motor and
possibly contractors pollution.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * geotechnical investigation report
  * loss schedule

Please confirm which carriers you are handling and provide claim references. Our
client's counsel is Marchetti, Oduya & Steinbrenner and they have asked to be
copied on the acknowledgement.

